    "created_at": "2020-08-21T18:51:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-21T18:51:57Z",
    "body": "Ideas dump:\r\n\r\n1. We do have conditional rendering of variables in the current framework. One option might be to define a set of special variables e.g. `starship_prefix_took` that are only defined when the module is not first in the render order.  \r\nThe serious downside here is that this is going to bloat the default format strings in the documentation and make them very difficult to understand, for what is essentially a 1-in-100 edge case.\r\n\r\n2. We could also add a prefix-flag to the format strings (so that you could specify that \"via\" is a prefix), but I'm not sure adding another piece of complexity into formatting strings for something like this is a good idea.\r\n\r\n3. Finally, we could just create a \"prefix\" field in the setting for each module that defines the prefix for that module using a format string. This has the advantage that anyone who wants to disable the prefixes can just put `prefix=\"\"` for all modules, but that would also require a pretty major overhaul. ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
